---
/**
 * ContactForm — the site's one contact form, reused on index.html, services.html (inside
 * ContactCTA), and contact.html.
 *
 * Source: components.md §4. Three fixes applied relative to the source markup, per the B2
 * brief:
 *
 * 1. ⚠️ NO WORKING ENDPOINT. The source form has no `action` attribute at all — Webflow's own
 *    backend intercepted submissions via `webflow.js` (excluded from this migration), so
 *    there is no working submit path anywhere in the exported markup. `action` below is a
 *    clearly-marked placeholder. **This is an open item, not a decision** — tracked in
 *    build-context/OPEN.md. Whoever closes it needs to supply a real endpoint (an Astro API
 *    route, a form service such as Formspree/Basin, or a serverless function) and update
 *    `action` (and possibly `method`) accordingly. `method="post"` is used here rather than
 *    the source's `method="get"` — GET would put a visitor's message text in the URL/server
 *    logs, which is inappropriate for a contact form; this is a corrected default, not a
 *    preserved one.
 *
 * 2. FIELD NAME CASING NORMALIZED. The source is internally inconsistent: index.html and
 *    services.html use `name`/`email`/`Message`; contact.html uses `Name`/`Email`/`Message`
 *    (and a different `id` on top, `Message-2`). Per the B2 brief this is normalized to
 *    lowercase everywhere — `name`, `email`, `message` — so a single endpoint sees one
 *    consistent payload shape regardless of which page the submission came from.
 *
 * 3. ACCESSIBILITY: the source has no `<label>` elements on any field (placeholder text
 *    stands in for a label on all three inputs) and no `required`/`aria-required` anywhere.
 *    Real, visible `<label>`s are added here, all three fields are marked required (a
 *    contact form with an empty message is not an actionable lead — a considered decision,
 *    not a ported one, since the source enforces no validation at all), and the
 *    success/error message blocks are wired as an `aria-live` region so assistive tech
 *    announces the outcome. Both regions exist in the static markup already (the source
 *    toggles their visibility via Webflow/JS); showing/hiding them on submit is an
 *    interaction and is explicitly out of scope for this phase (Phase E), so both start
 *    `hidden` here and are otherwise inert static markup.
 */
---

<div class="form-wrapper">
  <!--
    OPEN ITEM: no submit endpoint exists in the source export (see file header, point 1).
    Replace `action` below when a real endpoint is chosen — do not ship this placeholder.
  -->
  <form id="contact-form" name="contact-form" class="form" action="#contact-form-endpoint-todo" method="post">
    <div class="form-field-wrapper">
      <label for="name" class="form-label">Name</label>
      <input
        class="form-input"
        maxlength="256"
        name="name"
        id="name"
        placeholder="Your Name"
        type="text"
        required
        aria-required="true"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="form-field-wrapper">
      <label for="email" class="form-label">Email</label>
      <input
        class="form-input"
        maxlength="256"
        name="email"
        id="email"
        placeholder="Your Email"
        type="email"
        required
        aria-required="true"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="form-field-wrapper">
      <label for="message" class="form-label">Message</label>
      <textarea
        id="message"
        name="message"
        maxlength="5000"
        placeholder="Your Message"
        class="form-input is-text-area"
        required
        aria-required="true"></textarea>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="button primary submit-button">Submit</button>
  </form>
  <div class="form-message-success" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
    <p>Thank you! Your submission has been received!</p>
  </div>
  <div class="form-message-error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive" hidden>
    <p>Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .form-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .form-field-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xxs);
  }
  .form-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-looser);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .form-input {
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: var(--divider-width) solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--color-transparent);
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .form-input:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    background: var(--color-field-focus-bg);
  }
  .form-input.is-text-area {
    min-height: 8rem;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  .submit-button {
    /*
     * Source is a bare `<input type="submit">` styled `.button.primary.w-button` — NOT the
     * link-based `Button` component's DOM shape (no `.button-inner` wrapper, no hover-swap
     * span; see Button.astro's file header). Visual treatment duplicated here to match.
     */
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-on-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono-md);
    line-height: var(--lh-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: var(--space-xs) 0.6rem; /* .6rem is off-scale in source, no token — see Button.astro */
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .submit-button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .form-message-success,
  .form-message-error {
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }
  .form-message-success {
    border: var(--divider-width) solid var(--color-ink);
  }
  .form-message-error {
    border: var(--divider-width) solid var(--color-ink);
    background: var(--wf-error-bg);
  }
  .form-message-success p,
  .form-message-error p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
